{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:same-class-labeled-minimax",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For the explicit submodel \\(k=d_x=d_z=2\\), \\(L=2\\), \\(\\pi_0=0.1\\), and \\(\\sigma_0=0.1\\), uniformly for \\(g\\in(0,1/4]\\), the labeled upper and lower bounds on the same gap stratum imply that, for finite \\(0<c<C<\\infty\\),\n\\[\nc\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt n\\,g}\\right\\}\\le\\inf_{\\widetilde p_n}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M(g)}E_{Q_P^{(n)}}[\\lVert\\widetilde p_n-p^{\\uparrow}(P)\\rVert_1]\\le C\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt n\\,g}\\right\\}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(g\\)",
      "\\(c\\)",
      "\\(C\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\widetilde p_n\\)",
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M(g)\\)",
      "\\(Q_P^{(n)}\\)",
      "\\(p^{\\uparrow}(P)\\)",
      "\\(k\\)",
      "\\(d_x\\)",
      "\\(d_z\\)",
      "\\(L\\)",
      "\\(\\pi_0\\)",
      "\\(\\sigma_0\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:local-weight-experiment",
      "thm:labeled-weight-upper",
      "thm:matching-local-lower-bounds",
      "def:labeled-weight-estimator"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Put\n\\[\nr_{n,g}:=\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac1{\\sqrt n\\,g}\\right\\}\n\\]\nand define the same-class minimax risk\n\\[\nR_{n,g}:=\\inf_{\\widetilde p_n}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M(g)}\nE_{Q_P^{(n)}}\\!\\left[\n\\lVert\\widetilde p_n-p^{\\uparrow}(P)\\rVert_1\\right].                       \\tag{13}\n\\]\nLet \\(R_{n,g}^{\\mathrm{loc}}\\) denote the same expression with \\(\\mathcal M(g)\\) replaced by \\(\\mathcal L_{n,g}^{p}\\), without changing the measurable decision class.  By \\(\\mathrm{def:local\\text{-}weight\\text{-}experiment}\\),\n\\(\\mathcal L_{n,g}^{p}\\subseteq\\mathcal M(g)\\).  Therefore monotonicity of the supremum, followed by the labeled-coordinate inequality in \\(\\mathrm{thm:matching\\text{-}local\\text{-}lower\\text{-}bounds}\\), gives a constant \\(c_->0\\), independent of \\(n\\) and \\(g\\in(0,1/4]\\), such that\n\\[\nR_{n,g}\\ge R_{n,g}^{\\mathrm{loc}}\\ge c_-r_{n,g}.                          \\tag{14}\n\\]\nThe estimator \\(\\widehat p_n^{\\uparrow}\\) is a total Borel map into \\(\\Delta^{k-1}\\) by \\(\\mathrm{def:labeled\\text{-}weight\\text{-}estimator}\\), so it is an admissible competitor in (13).  The already proved theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:labeled\\text{-}weight\\text{-}upper}\\) supplies a finite constant \\(C_+>0\\), also independent of \\(n\\) and \\(g\\), for which\n\\[\nR_{n,g}\n\\le\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M(g)}E_{Q_P^{(n)}}\\!\\left[\n\\lVert\\widehat p_n^{\\uparrow}-p^{\\uparrow}(P)\\rVert_1\\right]\n\\le C_+r_{n,g}.                                                             \\tag{15}\n\\]\nSet \\(c:=\\min\\{c_-/2,C_+/2\\}\\) and \\(C:=C_+\\).  Then \\(0<c<C<\\infty\\), and (14)--(15) prove\n\\[\nc\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac1{\\sqrt n\\,g}\\right\\}\n\\le\\inf_{\\widetilde p_n}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M(g)}\nE_{Q_P^{(n)}}\\!\\left[\n\\lVert\\widetilde p_n-p^{\\uparrow}(P)\\rVert_1\\right]\n\\le C\\min\\left\\{1,\\frac1{\\sqrt n\\,g}\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThis is a same-class statement: the lower experiment is a subset of the very gap stratum over which the upper bound holds.",
    "justification": "This corollary makes the clipped inverse-gap rate a same-class minimax statement on the explicit parameter class containing the local path.",
    "gap": "VMW supplies separated recovery but not the factorization-preserving local converse that certifies the transition rate on the displayed class.",
    "consumer": "The frontier gives analysts a sharp threshold for when separate effect-ordered masses are statistically defensible.",
